# FUTURE ARCHITECTURE PRINCIPLES

Future Systems must adhere to:

* compatibility with existing architecture
* traceability to governance structure
* modular design assumptions
* non-disruptive integration potential
* clear separation from production systems

Future concepts must remain architecturally respectful of existing system boundaries.

---

# TRANSITION TO PRODUCTION

Future Systems may transition to production only if they:

* are fully specified
* pass testing (Series 704)
* pass validation (Series 705)
* comply with governance (Series 000)
* integrate with existing architecture (Series 200–700)
* demonstrate operational value

No Future System becomes active without formal elevation.

---

# GOVERNANCE

Future Systems shall never:

* bypass production controls
* assume automatic implementation
* disrupt existing architecture
* overwrite current operational systems
* introduce undocumented behavior into production

Future Systems exist for planning, not execution.

---

